OpenCPN 5.14.2 for AmigaOS 3: the deferred start-up, a debug check and the arch name.
- ocpn_frame.cpp: after the first-start wizard OpenCPN rebuilds the chart
  database and resumes its deferred start-up when the rebuild ends. With no
  chart folders no rebuild runs and nothing resumed it: the main window
  stayed blank, with no toolbar. The start-up now resumes at once.
- navutil_base.cpp: helpers made with wxString::FromUTF8 are empty where the
  build's character set cannot hold them, and Replace() of an empty string
  failed a debug check at start; they are skipped when empty.
- base_platform.cpp: the processor is m68k (it said i386).

Copyright (c) 2026 AmiCradle Team (these changes; GPL v2 or later, as OpenCPN)

--- a/gui/src/ocpn_frame.cpp
+++ b/gui/src/ocpn_frame.cpp
@@ -865,6 +865,11 @@
 
     LoadS57();
     ChartData->Create(ChartDirArray, pprog);
+  } else if (!g_bDeferredInitDone) {
+    // No chart folders yet (a first start where the wizard added none): no
+    // rebuild runs, so nothing would call FinalizeChartDBUpdate() to resume
+    // the deferred start-up, and it stopped here with a blank chart area.
+    if (gFrame) gFrame->InitTimer.Start(100, wxTIMER_ONE_SHOT);
   }
 }
 
